        inplace: can optionally do the operation in-place. Default: ``False``

    Shape:
        - Input: :math:`(*)`, where :math:`*` means any number of dimensions.
        - Output: :math:`(*)`, same shape as the input.

    .. image:: ../scripts/activation_images/CELU.png

    Examples::

        >>> m = nn.CELU()
        >>> input = torch.randn(2)
        >>> output = m(input)

